# Test: `ze cli -c` with a monitor, a chain and `| save` sends the typed line and saves only what the chain keeps
#
# The one question: when an operator runs `ze cli -c "monitor ... | match
# state | save events.log"`, does the client send the typed line with the
# rendering key, so the daemon accounts the line as typed and applies `match`,
# while the client formats and writes the file holding only the kept events?
# TestPresentationSuffixSameOnClientAndDaemon proves the split and
# TestExecSessionRendersStatement the key; only the two processes together
# prove which side selects, which side saves, and what is accounted.
#
# VALIDATES: spec-pipe-chain-honored-on-every-command-surface AC-23, AC-36
#   (the client half), user stories 7 and 12.
# PREVENTS: the client splitting the chain and sending `monitor ...` alone
#   (internal/component/cli/client/main.go StreamMonitor today), so accounting
#   records a line nobody typed and the client decides which rows it keeps.
#
# Red today: the ACCT START record is `monitor event include open,state`
#   with no chain. The file assertions pass today (the client filters and
#   saves); they must stay green when the daemon takes `match` over.
#
# Method: monitor-pipe-chain-ssh.ci's daemon and TACACS+ mock. `ze cli -c`
# runs in the background, ready once it prints the monitor's header (its
# subscription barrier, which `match state` keeps); then
# plugin/ssh-exec-line brings the dynamic BGP session up (its own monitor
# line only waits for the state event), wait-file.sh polls the save in
# progress for the state event, and the client is stopped with SIGTERM.
#
# A stream's `| save` is atomic (StreamSaves, internal/component/command
# pipe_save.go): the client writes a `.ze-save-*` temporary file beside the
# destination and renames it onto events.log only when the stream ends, so
# events.log does not exist while the monitor runs. The poll reads the
# temporary file; the assertions after the stop read events.log, which the
# terminate signal commits (StreamMonitor, internal/component/cli/client
# main.go), with no temporary file left.

option=timeout:value=90s
option=env:var=ZE_CONFIG_DIR:value=.
option=env:var=XDG_DATA_HOME:value=.
option=env:var=ze.ssh.password:value=testpass

stdin=init-answers:terminator=EOF_INIT
admin
testpass
127.0.0.1
$PORT2
EOF_INIT

tmpfs=monitor.conf:terminator=EOF_CONF
system {
	authentication {
		tacacs {
			server 127.0.0.1 { port $PORT; key "ze-mock-key"; }
			timeout 2
			authorization true
			accounting true
		}
		tacacs-profile 15 { profile [ admin ]; }
	}
	authorization {
		profile admin { run { default-action allow; } edit { default-action allow; } }
	}
}
environment {
	ssh {
		enabled true
		server main {
			ip 127.0.0.1;
			port $PORT2;
		}
	}
}
bgp {
	group dynamic-monitor {
		connection {
			remote {
				ip dynamic
				connect false
				range 127.0.0.1/32
			}
			local {
				ip 127.0.0.1
				port $PORT3
				accept true
			}
		}
		session {
			asn { local 65000; }
			router-id 1.1.1.1
			family {
				ipv4/unicast { prefix { maximum 10000; } }
			}
			capability { graceful-restart disable; }
		}
	}
}
EOF_CONF

cmd=background:seq=1:exec=le mock tacacs --port $PORT --key ze-mock-key --user admin:testpass:15:name=tacacs:ready=le mock tacacs: listening on
expect=stderr:pattern=ACCT START seq=[0-9]+ total=[0-9]+ cmd="monitor event include open,state \| match state \| save events.log"
reject=stderr:pattern=ACCT START .*cmd="monitor event include open,state"

cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=ze init:stdin=init-answers:exit=0
cmd=background:seq=3:exec=ze start monitor.conf:name=daemon:ready=Ze running.

cmd=background:seq=4:exec=ze cli -c "monitor event include open,state | match state | save events.log":name=client:ready=monitoring
cmd=foreground:seq=5:exec=le test fixture ui/await-save-file monitoring:timeout=40s:exit=0

cmd=foreground:seq=6:exec=le test fixture plugin/ssh-exec-line stream $PORT2 $PORT3 'monitor event include state' up -:timeout=45s
expect=exit:code=0

# The client formats each kept event before it saves it
# (internal/component/cli/client/main.go StreamMonitor, formatMonitorLine in
# internal/component/bgp/plugins/cmd/monitor/format.go), so the file holds
# one-liners, never the JSON: a state event is `---- STATE  <peer> <AS> up`.
cmd=foreground:seq=7:exec=le test fixture ui/await-save-file 'STATE.* up':timeout=40s:exit=0
cmd=stop:seq=8:name=client:signal=term

# Only what `match state` keeps was saved: no OPEN event reached the file. A
# saved OPEN is formatted `recv OPEN   <peer> ...` (formatOpen); the header
# names `open` in lower case, so the case-sensitive check reads ` OPEN `.
cmd=foreground:seq=9:exec=le test fixture ui/check-committed-save events.log 'STATE.* up' ' OPEN ':exit=0
expect=stdout:contains=OK: committed save events.log verified

cmd=stop:seq=10:name=daemon:signal=term
cmd=stop:seq=11:name=tacacs:signal=term
